    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0643" n="1433" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Dulles papers, “Telephone
                    Conversations”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d202-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1953-01-28">January 28,
                            1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <item>Participants:</item>
                    <item>Secretary Dulles</item>
                    <item>Senator Joseph R. McCarthy</item>
                </list>
                <p>Senator McCarthy telephoned the Secretary today to tell him that his Committee on
                    Government Operations is investigating the State Department’s filing system, but
                    not from the communism angle. If it discloses anything along that line it will
                    be referred to Sen. Jenner. He advised the Secretary that he would probably want
                    to call in someone from the Archives to set up a new system. The Secretary said
                    he knew from previous experience that once anything was filed here it was
                    lost.</p>
                <pb facs="0644" n="1434" xml:id="pg1434"/>
                <p>The Secretary told Senator McCarthy that he wanted all the help he could get and
                    if anything was discovered he wanted to know about it, but he wanted the thing
                    handled tactfully.</p>
                <p>The Senator said that he would like to see the Secretary after he returned from
                        Europe,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d202-f2"/> when he would have some concrete
                    suggestions, etc. The Secretary asked if he had discovered any evidence of bad
                    intent, and the Senator said that it was mostly wastefulness and
                    inefficiency.</p>
                <p>The conversation closed with the Senator repeating that he would try to see the
                    Secretary after his return.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d202-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d202-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Secretary Dulles’ personal secretary, Burnita O’Day, and by Special
                    Assistant to the Secretary of State Roderic L. O’Connor.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d202-f2" n="2" xml:id="d202-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation on the tour of European capitals by Secretary of State Dulles
                    and Mutual Security Director Harold Stassen, Jan. 31–Feb. 8, 1953, see <ref
                        target="frus1952-54v05p2#pg_1548">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>,
                        Part 2, pp. 1548</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
